# V1 Appointments + MCTB UI Rebuild

**UX/DESIGN HARD RULES:** `.cursor/rules/transovo-ux-governance.mdc` and all `transovo-*.mdc` standards — **mandatory** for any UI work. Not optional guides.

**Read first:** `docs/V1-APPOINTMENTS-MCTB-UI-REBUILD.md` (full spec + reuse map)

## Hard rules

1. **Do not delete** Campaigns, Drips, Keywords, Playbooks, Automations, bulk send, workers, or related routes/APIs — **hide from nav** only.
2. **Reuse before building** — audit existing Contacts, Conversations, SMS composer, templates, scheduler, compliance, MCTB components. No parallel appointment messaging system.
3. **Nav flags** — use `src/lib/products/v1-launch-nav.ts`; do not scatter hardcoded nav conditionals.
4. **MCTB** — tighten UI to match new shell; do not rebuild voice/SMS runtime. Keep both `press_1` and `existing_consent`.
5. **Appointments** — new surfaces required (`/appointments`, `/appointments/calendar`, `/appointments/types`). Reuse messaging + worker infra. `AppointmentType` ≠ `Appointment`.
6. **One product chrome** — single sidebar/header; operational dashboard; calendar stays visually sparse (Calendly/Google patterns for types, availability, preview, overlay detail).

## V1 primary nav

Overview · Appointments (Calendar, Scheduled, Types, Reminders) · Conversations · Contacts · Missed Calls · Analytics · Numbers · Compliance · Settings

## Hide from launch nav

Campaigns · Drips · Keywords · Playbooks · Automations · Grow · mass-SMS analytics · Smart Routing · AI Receptionist (routes preserved)

## Before coding UI changes

1. Audit existing routes/components  
2. Check reuse map in the doc (Appendix A)  
3. Consolidate nav/header first  
4. Browser + real SMS/MCTB E2E before declaring ready

## Do not build before launch

AI receptionist, mass SMS expansion, giant automation builder, fake integrations, payments (unless trivial), Calendly enterprise complexity.
